hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"430","Hannad ibn al-Sari and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Wa'il ibn Dawud: I heard al-Bahiyy say: When Ibrahim, son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died — he died at six months — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over him at the sitting places. Abu Dawud said: Hannad narrated: He is indeed truthful, and he indeed has a nursing mother in Paradise."
"431","I read to Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Talaqani: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to you, from Ya'qub ibn al-Qa'qa', from 'Ata', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over his son Ibrahim when he was seventy nights old."
"432","Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn 'Adi, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over those slain at Uhud."
"433","Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned two men between Makkah and Madinah; he prayed over one of them and did not pray over the other. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated connected (muttasil) with other wording."
